We provide specific examples illustrating the connection between Madsen-Weiss' classification of oriented diffeomorphism classes of homologically trivial 4-manifolds and the stable stable homotopy group of spheres, resulting from combining b-principle and stability theorems in a Pradines-like approach. These examples include: 
A. An alternative simplified proof for Madsen-Weiss' classification utilizing cobordism and stable homotopy theory simplifications; 
B. A generalization of Madsen-Weiss' classification to G-bundles over oriented 4-manifolds, with G being an orthogonal product of finite number of various simple compact Lie groups; 
C. A generalization of Parry-Simmons' four-manifolds homeomorphism topological criterion to compact oriented homeomorphic types. 
These results are grounded in a generalization of Hatcher's homotopy equivalence, involving the homotopy equivalence of compact orthogonal products of finite number of different simple compact Lie groups.
